  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request gen_ues229q turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "About that question — Got a read on anyone here yet? Who should I be watching?"
    YOU: "Still figuring everyone out."
    NPC: "Same. But keep your eyes open — some people here are performing, not surviving."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: They pull back half a step — not leaving, just... further.
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Watch the quiet ones. Not the loud — the loud tell you everything. The quiet are either thinking or planning, and you can't tell which until it matters."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on your read on people here."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Like I said — we're still on your read on people here."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on your read on people here. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Can I ask you something else?"
    NPC: "Never mind. You had something to say?"
    YOU: "People are going hungry. What do we do?"
    NPC: "My stomach's been talking louder than me lately. 10 of us are running on empty."
    YOU: "And then?"
    NPC: A neutral quiet returns, the kind where words land normally.
    YOU: "And then?"
    NPC: "Rest when you can. We'll talk again soon."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: They fill the quiet. "Anyway — where was I?"
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "Take care out there."

