  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request emma_larsen turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: Emma: "Don't just stand there — you've got opinions, right?"
    NPC: Emma seems lighter — something good landed recently.
    YOU: "How can I help?"
    NPC: "I still need help with the creek water run."
    YOU: "What did you see out there?"
    NPC: "This one is Jackfruit. Look at the leaf, feel the stem, breathe it in. It'll stick."
    YOU: "Tell me more."
    NPC: "No, really, it's fine. Forget I even asked."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "All sorted. Some things just work out."
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "It's handled. Really — it is. I appreciate you asking, though."
    YOU: "Tell me more."
    NPC: "That's the whole of it. Sorry."
    YOU: "Can I ask you something else?"
    NPC: "Right — go on, I'm listening."
    YOU: "What's new with you? Anything good, bad, or weird?"
    NPC: "You asked me that before. It's a different question now." "They say the table's coming. For us. I keep thinking about what we'd even bring to it."
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: The moment passes without landing. Not yet.
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "I could talk all day, but — go on. We'll talk more."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "...Think about it? I'll be around."
